Day 15 — Atomic Account Balance Operations
Objective

Implement safe debit and credit operations inside Account Service while preventing:

Negative balances
Duplicate balance updates
Concurrent double spending
Lost updates
Unauthorized updates to inactive accounts
Architecture Decision

Account Service is the sole owner of account balances.

Transaction Service must never update the ACCOUNTS table directly. It will call Account Service through an internal API.

Database Changes

Created Flyway migration:

V3__create_account_balance_operations.sql

Created table:

ACCOUNT_BALANCE_OPERATIONS

This immutable ledger stores:

Operation reference
Transaction reference
Account ID
Operation type
Amount
Balance before
Balance after
Request hash
Description
Creation timestamp

Supported operation types:

DEBIT
CREDIT
REVERSAL

REVERSAL is reserved for later compensation logic and cannot be submitted directly yet.

New Error Codes
ACC-006 — Insufficient funds
ACC-007 — Balance-operation idempotency conflict
ACC-008 — Balance operation not found
Pessimistic Locking

Added a pessimistic write-lock query to AccountRepository:

@Lock(LockModeType.PESSIMISTIC_WRITE)
@Query("""
        SELECT account
        FROM Account account
        WHERE account.accountId = :accountId
        """)
Optional<Account> findByIdForUpdate(
        @Param("accountId") Long accountId
);

This locks the account row while a balance operation is processed.

Concurrent requests for the same account must wait and are processed one at a time.

Balance Operation Workflow
Receive request
    ↓
Lock account row
    ↓
Generate request hash
    ↓
Check operation idempotency
    ↓
Validate account is ACTIVE
    ↓
Validate available balance
    ↓
Calculate new balance
    ↓
Update account balance
    ↓
Insert immutable ledger record
    ↓
Commit both changes together

The account update and ledger insertion execute inside one @Transactional method.

If either operation fails, both changes roll back.

Idempotency

Every balance request includes:

Operation-Reference

Example:

day15-account-21-debit-001

Behavior:

Same reference and same request: returns the original operation.
Same reference with different request data: returns ACC-007.
The balance is never updated twice for the same operation.

A SHA-256 request hash is generated using:

Account ID
Transaction reference
Operation type
Amount
Description
